      <title>US Stocks Set to Rebound After AI Selloff</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-23/daybreak-europe-11-23-2026-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">814e589449f7f11c428233e2</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:00:48 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Brussels, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

US equity-index futures rallied as buyers returned following Friday’s selloff in artificial intelligence companies. Treasury futures fell as demand for haven assets ebbed.

International climate talks collapsed on Sunday without any major agreement after dozens of countries rejected a deal they saw as pandering to the fossil fuel industry.

Plus, European natural gas prices jumped after temperature forecasts shifted sharply lower, which could put further pressure on inventories already depleted by export disruptions stemming from the US-Iran war.

Today's guest: Ian Horn, Portfolio Manager, Muzinich &amp; Co. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
